        "prompt": "Explain why every multiple of 4 is a multiple of 2.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Every multiple of $4$ equals $2\\times2n$, which is $2$ times a whole number.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4\\times n&=2\\times2\\times n\\\\&=2\\times2n\\end{align*}$$ Since $4=2\\times2$, every multiple of $4$ can be written as $2$ times the whole number $2n$. Therefore every multiple of $4$ is a multiple of $2$.",
